# Production review environment on Linux with Python 3.12.
# Regenerate requirements.txt with the command recorded in its header.
#
# peerreviewagents 0.10 runs the review as a Claude Code plugin, so the
# package carries no model client and the plain package is the whole
# dependency. There are no extras to ask for.
#
# 0.10.0 is not on PyPI, so the engine is pinned to the commit this repository
# is written for, as the GitHub archive of that commit. The lock carries the
# archive's sha256, so an install gets the engine this pipeline was tested
# against or it fails. A GitHub archive is generated rather than stored, so if
# one is ever regenerated differently the hash stops the install instead of
# letting a different engine through. To move to a new engine commit, change
# the sha here and recompile the lock with the command in its header.
peerreviewagents @ https://github.com/pgarrett-scripps/PeerReviewAgents/archive/9c362836e575e53a2ad5a83a8bbd2859119863eb.tar.gz
rustypaper==0.2.4
pyyaml>=6.0
